<title>THAILAND: Thai rice vessels loading and movements at Nov 29.</title>
<headline>Thai rice vessels loading and movements at Nov 29.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Thai Commerce Ministry</p>
<p>detailed rice loading at Thai ports as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>Vessel		Date of Arrival   Quantity     Destination</p>
<p>Asian Progress    01/11/96	     11,000	  Nigeria</p>
<p>Sangthai Glory    07/11/96		N/A	    Singapore</p>
<p>Sortume Navigator 07/11/96		5,000	  China</p>
<p>Vinh Thuob	  11/11/96		N/A	    China</p>
<p>Silver Sua	  11/11/96		4,200	  China</p>
<p>Dibena Express    13/11/96		5,000	  India</p>
<p>Anda Jang	   15/11/96		1,000	  China</p>
<p>Stamon		15/11/96		6,000	  Africa</p>
<p>Budi Ainna	  15/11/96		3,800	  Malaysia</p>
<p>Sangthai Venus    18/11/96		4,000	  Singapore</p>
<p>Was Yee	     18/11/96		3,000	  China</p>
<p>Iran Sabr	   18/11/96		9,000	  Iran</p>
<p>Princess of Lorne 18/11/96	     10,000	  Philippines</p>
<p>Jin Csuah	   18/11/96		4,000	  China</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
